# Rover P5B 3.5 Litre four-door saloon, 1967-1973.
#
# The P5 with the ex-Buick V8: 4,724 mm long, 1,778 mm wide, 1,460 mm high,
# 2,794 mm wheelbase. The car of government ministers and police chief constables;
# a four-door saloon with a cramped boot and a column change on early cars.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P5
#
# Colours: Arden Green, Sierra Beige, Mexico Brown and Black are documented Rover
# finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 100 in total (green 32, beige 26, brown 22, black 20).
#
# Speed 180 km/h; comfort 120/510 (line). Classes 2,3.
# Dates: 1967-1973 with a road tail to about 1986.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p5b.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p5b/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RoverP5B(ArdenGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=32
intro_year=1967
intro_month=9
retire_year=1986
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=120
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=510

